contributions.text:
{
  "reading": "Asked: does Vito, Fanatic of Aclazotz earn a slot on threat-v1, and how often does it reach its third trigger (the 4/3 flyer). It is a good thesis fit: it pays on Treasure, Blood and fetchland sacrifices that nothing in the list pays on today, and it turns fodder into a flying threat. That answers the log's repeated 'rebuilds into blockers, not threats'. But its first two tiers repeat Vraan, Executioner Thane (2 mana, once a turn, drain 2 and gain 2 off any death), and it closes neither short axis (card-advantage 7 against 10, ramp 8 against 10). The goldfish floor against the best slot is small (+0.6 pts killed by T10). Recommendation: NO CHANGE. If the pilot wants it, Twilight Prophet is the slot.",
  "log_entries_read": ["001", "002", "003", "006", "007", "008"],
  "axes_engaged": [
    {"axis": "card-advantage", "verdict": "weakness", "measured": {"value": 7}, "reading": "Under the target of 10. Vito draws nothing, and the cheapest slot by the goldfish (Twilight Prophet) is a draw engine."},
    {"axis": "ramp", "verdict": "weakness", "measured": {"value": 8}, "reading": "Under the target of 10. Vito does not touch it."},
    {"axis": "threat-density", "verdict": "strength", "measured": {"value": 20}, "reading": "Twenty against a floor of 3. Vito would be one more payoff on an axis that is already full."}
  ],
  "sacrifice_count": {
    "set": "every threat-v1 card whose text makes YOU sacrifice another permanent (oracle regex 'sacrific|Treasure|Blood token|Clue|Food', read card by card)",
    "free_unbounded_outlets": ["Ashnod's Altar", "Viscera Seer", "Yahenni, Undying Partisan", "Vish Kal, Blood Arbiter"],
    "once_per_turn_tap_outlets": ["Phyrexian Tower", "Master of Dark Rites"],
    "mana_costed_repeatable": ["Edgar, Ancient Bloodlord ({2})", "Anje, Maid of Dishonor ({2}, creature or Blood)", "Erebos, Bleak-Hearted ({1}{B})", "Kalitas, Traitor of Ghet ({2}{B}, Vampire or Zombie only)"],
    "one_shot": ["Selfless Spirit (itself)", "Bloodtithe Harvester (itself, sorcery speed)", "Diabolic Intent (cost)", "Liliana, Dreadhorde General -4 (you sacrifice two: two triggers)"],
    "noncreature_fodder": {"treasure": ["Pitiless Plunderer (one per other creature death)", "Black Market Connections (one a turn)"], "blood": ["Anje, Maid of Dishonor (once a turn)", "Bloodtithe Harvester (on entry)"], "sac_lands": ["Arid Mesa", "Bloodstained Mire", "Marsh Flats", "Verdant Catacombs", "Wooded Foothills", "Silent Clearing ({1})"], "clues_food": []},
    "not_sacrifice": ["Skullclamp (equip)", "Lethal Scheme and Clever Concealment (convoke taps)", "The Meathook Massacre and Toxic Deluge (-X/-X, not sacrifice)", "Crackling Doom (opponents sacrifice)"],
    "per_turn": "With a free outlet and three bodies, three sacrifices is trivial on any turn. Ashnod's Altar is mana-positive, and Plunderer makes each body two sacrifices (body, then its Treasure). Without one, a turn reaches about one to two: Black Market Connections' Treasure, one Tower or Master tap, and a costed outlet at {2}. A third costs two to four more mana. The counter resets on every player's turn, so an instant-speed outlet gets the first-tier 2 life on each opponent's turn too.",
    "how_often": "My hypergeometric over the 99 (not an artifact figure): at least one of the 4 free outlets in 12 cards is 41%, and 55% with Tower and Master of Dark Rites added. Vito himself must also be drawn and live. So the 4/3 is a most-turns event in the minority of games with an outlet and Vito both down, and rare otherwise. The goldfish's own count is lower still: cumulative mean sacrifices 0.551 by T6, 1.452 by T8, 3.368 by T10. It does not model Plunderer's or Black Market Connections' Treasure (goldfish_metrics.meta.treasure_sources_not_modelled)."
  },
  "cut_candidates": [
    {"card": "Twilight Prophet", "why": "The cheapest slot by the goldfish: Vito for it reads 10 better, 0 worse. Killed by T10 +0.6 pts [+0.4, +0.7], damage @T10 +0.9 [+0.8, +1.0], extra cards by T8 +0.02 [+0.01, +0.02]. This is a FLOOR, because Vito's trigger is unmodelled.", "cost_of_cutting": "A draw and each-opponent drain engine every upkeep once the deck has ten permanents. Draw is the axis the pilot calls required ('runs out of steam post T7/8'), and card-advantage is already 7 against 10. The goldfish shows no draw loss, which more likely means it rarely reaches the blessing than that the draw is worthless.", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty": "painful"},
    {"card": "Malakir Bloodwitch", "why": "A 5-mana one-shot drain against a 4-mana repeatable one. The goldfish reads it as a trade, a floor: 4 better, 3 worse. Life lost outside combat @T10 -1.2 [-1.4, -1.1], killed outside combat by T10 -0.7 pts [-0.9, -0.5], life gained by T8 -0.34 [-0.39, -0.30].", "cost_of_cutting": "The branch's Vampire-count finisher, which the pilot approved on 2026-11-20 as 'the thesis in one card'. Cutting it reverses a four-day-old call, and the goldfish reads a loss on the drain rows.", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty": "contested"},
    {"card": "Bloodline Keeper", "why": "Another 4-mana Vampire flyer. The goldfish withheld its rows as BLIND because it does not read Keeper's tokens.", "cost_of_cutting": "A fodder engine: a 2/2 flying Vampire every turn, doubled by Anointed Procession or Elspeth, then a +2/+2 lord. Cutting the thing Vito eats to make room for Vito works against itself.", "orphans_stack": [], "difficulty": "painful"}
  ],
  "add_candidates": [
    {"card": "Vito, Fanatic of Aclazotz", "closes": "threat-density", "source": "prompt", "why": "A fit, not a fix. It pays on 2 Treasure makers, 2 Blood makers and 6 sac-lands that no payoff in the list sees today. Its first-tier gain feeds Vito Thorn, Sanguine Bond, Enduring Tenacity, Blight-Priest and Oathsworn's recast. Its third tier answers 'rebuilds into blockers, not threats' (log 001/002/003/006). Its tiers cap at three a turn and it appears in 0 Commander Spellbook records, so it adds no infinite, two-card or otherwise. It is not a Game Changer.", "natural_cut": "Twilight Prophet"}
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    {"question": "How often does a real threat-v1 game have a free outlet, Vito and three sacrifices on one turn?", "settled_by": "goldfish", "why_it_matters": "The 4/3 is the only part of Vito that Vraan does not already do. Until the goldfish models Vito's trigger and the Plunderer and Black Market Connections Treasure, every row is a floor."},
    {"question": "Does Twilight Prophet reach the city's blessing by T6 in threat-v1, and how much does it draw?", "settled_by": "goldfish", "why_it_matters": "The goldfish reads no draw loss from cutting it. That is either true or a sign the blessing is under-read, and it decides whether this cut is painful or easy."}
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "Vito's drain and token are unmodelled (classify reads drain: unmodelled), so every row above is a floor for Vito, not the reason.",
    "The 41%/55% outlet odds are my hypergeometric over enumerated cards, not an artifact figure. The free-outlet group rate in CONTEXT (55% by T6) is for v3.0.0, not threat-v1.",
    "Study 013's facts show a -9.92 damage @T10 row from the study's own null-out screen. That is not one of the three swaps above and was not used."
  ]
}
